#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# scorer_gi

#% text
# `scorer_gi(z)` gives the Scorer function `Gi(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `Gi(z) = Bi(z) - Hi(z)` is a solution of the inhomogeneous Airy equation `w'' - z w = -1/pi` (DLMF 9.12).

#% item
# `Gi(0) = Bi(0)/3`; `Gi(x)` tends to 0 at both ends of the real line, like `1/(pi x)`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values, by the Maclaurin series of `Hi` at a working precision that covers the cancellation of `Bi - Hi`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
scorer_gi(5.0)
#% output
#= 0.06491978409385311

#% cell
n(scorer_gi(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= 0.2384894214372833303739938866807654

#% cell
scorer_gi(0.2 + 1.0*im)
#% output
#= 0.368791881947282 + 0.04259021009349048im

#% cell
scorer_gi(0)
#% output
#= 3^(5/6)/(9*gamma(2/3))

#% text
# The value tends to `1/(pi x)` for large `x`:

#% cell
scorer_gi(50.0)*pi*50.0
#% output
#= 1.000016002561148

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `scorer_hi`, `scorer_gi_prime`, `airy_bi`, `airy_ai`
